|towns=[[Tavistock]]|previous=[[Torridge and West Devon (UK Parliament constituency)|Torridge and West Devon]] & [[South West Devon (UK Parliament constituency)|South West Devon]]}}'''Torridge and Tavistock''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=South West {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/south-west/ |access-date=2023-06-20 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it was first contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-01-19 |title=Have your say on major new boundary changes for Devon |url=https://www.tavistock-today.co.uk/news/have-your-say-on-major-new-boundary-changes-for-devon-512011 |access-date=2023-07-29 |website=Tavistock Times Gazette}}</ref>

== Boundaries ==
The constituency will be composed of the following (as they existed on 1 December 2020):

* The District of [[Torridge District|Torridge]].
* The Borough of [[West Devon]] wards of: [[Bere Ferrers]]; [[Bridestowe]]; [[Dartmoor]]; [[Mary Tavy]]; Milton Ford; Tamarside; [[Tavistock|Tavistock North; Tavistock South East; Tavistock South West]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 7 South West region}}</ref>

It will comprise the bulk of the current [[Torridge and West Devon (UK Parliament constituency)|Torridge and West Devon]] seat (to be abolished) - excluding the West Devon Borough wards of Buckland Monachorum and Burrator in the south, which will be transferred to [[South West Devon (UK Parliament constituency)|South West Devon]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Torridge and Tavistock |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Torridge%20and%20Tavistock |access-date=2023-07-29 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>

The previous MP for Torridge and West Devon was [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative Party]] member [[Geoffrey Cox (British politician)|Sir Geoffrey Cox KC]], who served from 5 May 2005 until the seat's abolition in 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Parliamentary career for Sir Geoffrey Cox - MPs and Lords |url=https://members.parliament.uk/member/1508/career |access-date=7 June 2024 |website=UK Parliament }}</ref>

