The 12 vote majority in Torbay was originally the second smallest in any of the 659 constituencies contested at the 1997 general election, with only the Liberal Democrats' majority of 2 in [[Winchester (UK Parliament constituency)|Winchester]] being smaller. However the Winchester result was subsequently challenged and declared void resulting in a [[1997 Winchester by-election|by-election]].<ref name="TimesGuide1997p299">{{cite book |title=The Times Guide to the House of Commons 1997 |date=1997 |publisher=Times Books |location=London |isbn=0-7230-0956-2 |page=299}}</ref>

