Another General Election was required to take place before the end of 1940. The political parties had been making preparations for an election to take place and by the Autumn of 1939, the following candidates had been selected; *'''Conservative''': [[Angus Hambro]] *'''Liberal''': [[Frank Byers]]<ref>The Liberal Magazine, 1939</ref> *'''Labour''': CL Lander<ref>Report of the Annual Conference of the Labour Party, 1939</ref>
