===Election in the 1940s=== {{Election box begin|title=[[1945 United Kingdom general election|General election 1945]]: Cheltenham<ref name="auto">British parliamentary election results, 1918–1949 (Craig)</ref> }} {{Election box winning candidate with party link| |party = Independent Conservative |candidate = [[Daniel Lipson]] |votes = 16,081 |percentage = 43.3 |change = ''N/A'' }} {{Election box candidate with party link |party = Labour Party (UK) |candidate = Phyllis Maude Warner |votes = 11,095 |percentage = 29.9 |change = +0.4 }} {{Election box candidate with party link |party = Conservative Party (UK) |candidate = [[W. W. Hicks Beach]] |votes = 9,972 |percentage = 26.8 |change = -45.7 }} {{Election box majority |votes = 4,986 |percentage = 13.4 |change = -27.6 }} {{Election box turnout |votes = 37,148 |percentage = 75.4 |change = +5.0 }} {{Election box Registered electors| |reg. electors =49,282 |percentage = 100.0 |change = +29.9 }} {{Election box hold with party link |winner = Independent Conservative |swing = +7.6 }} {{Election box end}} '''General Election 1939–40''':
Another General Election was required to take place before the end of 1940. The political parties had been making preparations for an election to take place from 1939 and by the end of this year, the following candidates had been selected; *'''Independent Conservative''': [[Daniel Lipson]] *'''Conservative''': C L Hargreaves<ref>Cheltenham Chronicle, 25 February 1939</ref> *'''Labour''': [[John Baird (Wolverhampton MP)|John Baird]]<ref>Cheltenham Chronicle, 20 January 1939</ref>
