'''General Election 1914–15'''
A general election was due to take place by the end of 1915. By the autumn of 1914, the following candidates had been selected to contest that election. Due to the outbreak of war, the election never took place; *'''Liberal Party''': [[Sir Henry Webb, 1st Baronet|Henry Webb]] *'''Labour Party''': [[James Wignall]]
