{{Short description|Parliamentary constituency in the United Kingdom, 2024 onwards}} {{Infobox UK constituency main|name=Glastonbury and Somerton|parliament=uk|year=[[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024]]|abolished=|type=County|previous=[[Somerton and Frome (UK Parliament constituency)|Somerton and Frome]], [[Wells (UK Parliament constituency)|Wells]] & [[Yeovil (UK Parliament constituency)|Yeovil]]|next= |electorate= 70,015 (2023)<ref>{{cite web |url= https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-two-constituency-names-designations-and-composition/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-two-constituency-names-designations-and-composition-south-west/#lg_glastonbury-and-somerton-cc-70015 |title= The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume two: Constituency names, designations and composition – South West |publisher=Boundary Commission for England |access-date=27 June 2024 |df=dmy }}</ref> |mp=[[To be confirmed|TBC]] |party=[[To be confirmed|TBC]]|region=England |county=[[Somerset]] |european= |elects_howmany=One|towns=[[Glastonbury]], [[Street, Somerset|Street]], [[Somerton, Somerset|Somerton]], [[Wincanton]]|caption2=Boundary of Glastonbury and Somerton in South West England|image2=[[File:South West England - Glastonbury and Somerton constituency.svg|255px|alt=Map of constituency]]}}'''Glastonbury and Somerton''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=South West {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/south-west/ |access-date=2023-06-20 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2022-11-08 |title=Shake-up revealed for Somerset MPs' boundaries |language=en-GB |work=BBC News |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-somerset-63557308 |access-date=2023-12-02}}</ref>
== Boundaries == {{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Glastonbury and Somerton (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}} The constituency will be composed of the following wards (as they existed on 1 December 2020):
* The District of Mendip wards of: Butleigh and Baltonsborough; Glastonbury St. Benedict’s; Glastonbury St. Edmund’s; Glastonbury St. John’s; Glastonbury St. Mary’s; Street North; Street South; Street West. * The District of South Somerset wards of: Blackmoor Vale; Bruton; Burrow Hill; Camelot; Cary; Curry Rivel, Huish & Langport; Hamdon; Islemoor; Martock; Milborne Port; Northstone, Ivelchester & St. Michael’s; Tower; Turn Hill; Wessex; Wincanton.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 7 South West region}}</ref>
It will be made up of the following areas of [[Somerset]]:<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Glastonbury and Somerton |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=glastonbury%20and%20somerton |access-date=2023-12-02 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>
* Majority of the current [[Somerton and Frome (UK Parliament constituency)|Somerton and Frome constituency]] (to be abolished, with remaining parts being included in the new [[Frome and East Somerset (UK Parliament constituency)|Frome and East Somerset]] seat). Includes the communities of [[Bruton]], [[Castle Cary]], [[Langport]], [[Martock]], [[Somerton, Somerset|Somerton]] and [[Wincanton]]. * [[Glastonbury]] and [[Street, Somerset|Street]] from the [[Wells (UK Parliament constituency)|Wells constituency]] (to be abolished and succeeded by [[Wells and Mendip Hills (UK Parliament constituency)|Wells and Mendip Hills]]) * A small part of the [[Yeovil (UK Parliament constituency)|Yeovil constituency]]. With effect from 1 April 2023, the Districts of Mendip and South Somerset were abolished and absorbed into the new unitary authority of Somerset.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Somerset (Structural Changes) Order 2022 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2022/329/contents/made}}</ref> The constituency will therefore now comprise the following electoral divisions of Somerset from the 2024 general election:
* Castle Cary; Curry Rivel and Langport; Glastonbury; Martock; Somerton; Street; Wincanton and Bruton; and small parts of Brympton, Coker, Mendip South, and South Petherton and Islemoor.<ref name=":0" />
==Constituency profile== [[Electoral Calculus]] characterises the proposed seat as "Strong Right", with right-wing economic and social views, high home ownership levels and strong support for Brexit.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Glastonbury%20and%20Somerton | title=Electoral Calculus }}</ref>
