|party=[[To be confirmed|TBC]]|region=England|county=[[Wiltshire]]|european=|elects_howmany=One|towns=[[Amesbury]], [[Marlborough, Wiltshire|Marlborough]]|image2=[[File:South West England - East Wiltshire constituency.svg|255px|alt=Map of constituency]]|caption2=Boundary of East Wiltshire in South West England}}'''East Wiltshire''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2022-11-09 |title=How Wiltshire constituency boundaries could change |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-wiltshire-63561333 |access-date=2023-07-21 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=South West {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/south-west/ |access-date=2023-06-20 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref>

== Boundaries ==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/East Wiltshire (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}}
The constituency will be composed of:

* The following wards of the [[Borough of Swindon]] (as they existed on 1 December 2020): Chiseldon and Lawn (polling district CLB); Ridgeway; Wroughton and Wichelstowe.
* The following electoral divisions of [[Wiltshire]] (as they existed on 4 May 2021): Aldbourne & Ramsbury; Amesbury East & Bulford; Amesbury South; Amesbury West; Avon Valley; Durrington; Ludgershall North & Rural; Marlborough East; Marlborough West; Pewsey; Pewsey Vale East; Pewsey Vale West; Tidworth East & Ludgershall South; Tidworth North & West; Till Valley.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 7 South West region}}</ref>

It will comprise the following areas:<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Wiltshire East |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Wiltshire+East |access-date=2024-02-25 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>

* The majority of the (to be abolished) [[Devizes (UK Parliament constituency)|Devizes constituency]] but excluding the town of [[Devizes]] and the area surrounding it, which will be included in the newly created constituency of [[Melksham and Devizes (UK Parliament constituency)|Melksham and Devizes]]; in this eastern part of Wiltshire, the largest settlement is [[Marlborough, Wiltshire|Marlborough]]
* In the north, an area transferred from [[South Swindon (UK Parliament constituency)|South Swindon]] which includes [[Wroughton]] and [[Chiseldon]]
* In the south, an area transferred from [[Salisbury (UK Parliament constituency)|Salisbury]] which includes [[Tilshead]], [[Shrewton]] and [[Amesbury]]

